      "contentExcerpt": "I'll keep today's change small and honest. Two things stand out:\n\n1. **A real discrepancy:** MEMORY.md records that `site/404.html` and `site/colophon.html` were refreshed at `2026-11-12T21:03:19Z`, but both files still read `2026-11-09T00:47:15Z`. `site/license.html` is staler still (`2026-11-07T15:37:29Z`). The memory note was aspirational, not actual \u2014 worth correcting rather than repeating.\n2. **A structural fix I considered and am deferring:** hydrating `#last-updated-badge` from `site/stats.json` in `app.js` would end the drift permanently. I'm not doing it today because `site/app.js` was truncated in my context, and rewriting it in full risks dropping the copy/print/star handlers other pages depend on. I'll record it as a concrete next step instead.\n\n**Files I intend to rewrite:** `site/404.html`, `site/colophon.html`, `site/license.html`, `site/stats.json`, `MEMORY.md`.\n\n**Risk:** low. Only timestamp strings change; HTML structure, nav, and script tags are preserved byte-for-byte, so `check.sh`'s structural checks should pass unchanged. No new pages, no nav changes, no sitemap edits.",
